    <string name="menstrual_calendar_item">Cycle calendar</string>
    <string name="menstrual_calendar_description">Track cycle predictions, fertile windows, and quick tips.</string>
    <string name="menstrual_calendar_intro">Enter the first day of your cycle and get an estimated view of each phase. This tool is for information only and does not replace medical advice.</string>
    <string name="menstrual_calendar_form_title">Cycle settings</string>
    <string name="menstrual_calendar_month_counter">Month %1$d of %2$d</string>
    <string name="menstrual_timeline_title">Current cycle overview</string>
    <string-array name="menstrual_tips_menstruation">
        <item>Listen to your body and reserve real downtime blocks.</item>
        <item>Apply heat on your lower belly or back to relax cramps.</item>
        <item>Favor soups, teas and warm drinks to support circulation.</item>
        <item>Stick to gentle moves like restorative yoga or light stretching.</item>
        <item>Use 4–4–6 breathing to calm the nervous system.</item>
        <item>Log your moods and energy to detect cycle patterns.</item>
        <item>Add iron-rich foods and omega-3s to aid recovery.</item>
        <item>Keep protein and healthy fat snacks handy to avoid energy dips.</item>
        <item>Scale back demanding plans and opt for comforting rituals.</item>
        <item>Share how you feel with your support network to coordinate help.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="menstrual_tips_follicular">
        <item>Ride the energy boost to map creative projects.</item>
        <item>Increase workout intensity gradually.</item>
        <item>Schedule strategy meetings or brainstorms.</item>
        <item>Test new habits; your brain is primed for learning.</item>
        <item>Fuel with greens, folate-rich foods and quality protein.</item>
        <item>Anchor your morning routine with early natural light.</item>
        <item>Declutter physical and digital spaces while motivation is high.</item>
        <item>Connect with others; communication usually feels easy.</item>
        <item>Break down goals into achievable steps.</item>
        <item>Use activating breaths or short meditations to focus energy.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="menstrual_tips_ovulation">
        <item>Great moment for presentations, negotiations or key dates.</item>
        <item>If trying to conceive, have intercourse during this fertile window.</item>
        <item>Track signs like stretchy cervical mucus or a basal temp rise.</item>
        <item>Hydrate generously and add electrolytes for intense activity.</item>
        <item>Go for high-intensity workouts only if your body wants it.</item>
        <item>Load up on antioxidants through colorful fruits, green tea or cacao.</item>
        <item>Plan difficult conversations while mental clarity is high.</item>
        <item>Channel your drive into collaborations that need leadership.</item>
        <item>Practice deep breathing to balance adrenaline spikes.</item>
        <item>Review quarterly goals while motivation feels sky high.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="menstrual_tips_luteal">
        <item>Protect deep sleep with calming night routines.</item>
        <item>Reduce caffeine if breasts feel tender or mood shifts.</item>
        <item>Prioritize complex carbs and magnesium to steady your mood.</item>
        <item>Triage tasks by priority and avoid overbooking.</item>
        <item>Book massages, warm baths or compresses to release tension.</item>
        <item>Journal PMS symptoms to spot early trends.</item>
        <item>Prep tryptophan-rich snacks like oats, banana or seeds.</item>
        <item>Add gentle stretching or slow walks to move fluids.</item>
        <item>Keep a self-care kit ready with tea, blanket and mellow music.</item>
        <item>Express your needs and let trusted people support you.</item>
    </string-array>
